Z||000021||Kelvin Vivian||06-06-2001||02:28 AM||||Here's a list of Fiero production numbers:<P>84 Indy Pace Car: 2,000<BR>84 Base Coupe: 7,099<BR>84 Sport Coupe: 62,070<BR>84 SE: 65,671<BR>Total 84 Production: 136,843<P>85 Base Coupe: 5,280<BR>85 Sport Coupe: 23,823<BR>85 SE 4-cyl: 12,901<BR>85 SE V6: 11,833<BR>85 GT: 22,534<BR>Total 85 Production: 76,371<P>86 Base Coupe: 9,143<BR>86 Sport Coupe: 24,866<BR>86 SE 4-cyl: 4,031<BR>86 SE V6: 28,274<BR>86 GT: 17,655<BR>Total 86 Production: 83,969<P>87 Base Coupe: 23,603<BR>87 Sport Coupe: 3,135<BR>87 SE 4-cyl: 1,401<BR>87 SE V6: 2,474<BR>87 GT: 15,966<BR>Total 87 Production: 46,579<P>88 Coupe: 13,910<BR>88 Formula: 5,684<BR>88 GT: 6,849<BR>Total 88 Production: 24,601<P>Some Fiero Colors:<BR>YELLOW - 1,166 (88 only) (489 coupe + 436 Formula + 241 GT)<BR>GOLD - 20,444 (86 16,325 + 87 4119)<BR>BLUE - 4,458 (87 only)<BR>MED RED METALLIC - 22,993 (87 20,264 + 88 2,729)<P>----------------------------------<P>Lizzy,<P>As TarHeelsFieros[Lisa] mentioned, the Fiero you have is 1 of 1,401 87 SE 4-cyls. And BLUE is the 2nd rarest Fiero color. <P>In 1987:<BR>- the Fiero gas tank was increased from 10.2 gal to 11.9 gal<BR>- the headlight motor/assembly was revised<BR>- the 4-cyl engine was changed to run with a single belt, and the ignition setup was revised<BR>- the rear decklid only has "Fiero" - no more 2M4/2M6 designations, makes it pretty much impossible to distinguish a SE 4-cyl and a SE V6 without popping the rear decklid.<P>84/85 SEs have what I like to call the "classic" or "original" Fiero body.<P>86/87 SEs have what I like to call the "aero package", which is the same body style as the 84 Indy Fiero and 85 GT.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
